  "Question": "If \\(a \\ast b = \\dfrac{a\\times b}{a+b}\\) for \\(a,\\) \\(b\\) positive integers, then what is \\(5 \\ast 10?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{3}{10} \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 1 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 2 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{10}{3} \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 50 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The rule says to multiply the two inputs and divide by their sum. Substituting \\(a=5\\) and \\(b=10\\) gives\n\\[\n5\\ast10=\\frac{5\\times10}{5+10}\n=\\frac{50}{15}=\\boxed{\\frac{10}{3}}.\n\\]\nThe denominator is 15, so the expression is defined. The last fraction comes from dividing numerator and denominator by 5. The answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
